      "turn": 1,
      "doctor_question": "Hello, welcome. What brings you into the clinic today?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S022",
      "patient_response": "I guess what brings me in is... well, I got really worked up in a staff meeting the other day. I started acting out this whole fall-prevention drill, you know? Like, moving chairs around, waving my arms everywhere, really getting into it. And I couldn't seem to stop, even when folks told me to sit down. It was just... I had to show them. You know, working as a personal care aide, falls are a big deal. My buddy Dave, he slipped on some ice last winter—not at work, just outside his apartment—and he broke his collarbone. He was out of work for weeks, and his dog, this little terrier mix, got so anxious with him just sitting around in a sling. I used to go over and walk the dog for him. Buster, that was his name. Good dog, but he pulled on the leash like you wouldn't believe. Anyway, yeah, the meeting... they said I was being disruptive.",
