    {
      "turn": 2,
      "doctor_question": "How has your sleep been lately?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S036",
      "patient_response": "Sleep? Oh, well... I've been sleeping maybe two, three hours a night. I'll wake up way before dawn, and honestly, I feel completely fine. Ready to go, you know? I don't see the problem with being up while the house is still dark, just... making plans, getting things organized. It's actually really quiet then. The streetlights outside my window have this weird orange glow, and sometimes I watch the moths bumping against the glass. There was this one moth last week, huge thing, looked almost like a bat. Reminded me of when I went camping with my uncle when I was a kid. We pitched this tent out by Lake George, and the mosquitoes were just eating us alive. He had this citronella candle that smelled like burnt lemon, and we tried to make s'mores, but the marshmallows kept catching on fire. I always liked mine a little charred anyway. But yeah, I wake up early, feel great, and just start planning out my day.",
