    {
      "turn": 3,
      "doctor_question": "Have you ever had a period in your life where you felt the complete opposite—feeling deeply down, depressed, or having very low energy for weeks at a time?",
      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "Down? No, I don't think so. I mean, I've had days where I didn't want to go into work, but who hasn't, right? Especially when Mrs. Higgins is on the schedule. She's this client I had, real sweet lady most of the time, but she insisted on watching these old black-and-white westerns all afternoon. The volume had to be all the way up because her hearing aids were always acting up. I tried telling her daughter about getting them checked, but the daughter lives out in Ohio somewhere. Cleveland, I think. Or maybe Columbus. I had a buddy who moved to Columbus for a girl, and they ended up breaking up before he even unpacked his boxes. He had to drive a U-Haul all the way back in a snowstorm. Have you ever driven a U-Haul? They handle like a boat, just swaying all over the highway. But yeah, no, I don't really get down like that. I just keep moving.",
