    {
      "turn": 4,
      "doctor_question": "Have you been taking any recreational drugs, new medications, or stimulants lately?",
      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "Drugs? No, no, I don't mess with any of that stuff. No new medications either. I mean, I drink coffee, if that counts as a stimulant? Though lately I haven't even really needed it. I used to drink those huge energy drinks, though, you know, the ones in the tall black cans with the bright green claw marks on them? My buddy Dave—the one with Buster, the dog I was telling you about—he used to drink like four of those a day when we were working third shift at this auto parts warehouse a few years back. \n\nThat place was freezing, man. They kept the giant shipping bay doors open even in November, and the wind would just whip right through the aisles. I had to wear these thick thermal socks, the heavy wool ones my Aunt Carol got me for Christmas. She knits them herself, which is real nice of her, but she uses the scratchiest yarn you've ever felt in your life. You have to wash them like three or four times with extra fabric softener before you can even put them on your feet without going crazy. And fabric softener is getting so expensive now, have you noticed? I was at the grocery store on Tuesday and a regular bottle was almost ten bucks. It's just soap for your clothes, it shouldn't cost that much. But yeah, no, no drugs or anything like that for me.",
